  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Tumonoic acid C may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Tumonoic acid C is predicted to act as a target for Leukocyte antigen CD37, which in turn is targeted by (11Bs)-7,11-Dihydroxy-3,4,9,11B-Tetramethyl-1H-Naphtho[2,1-F][1]Benzofuran-2,6-Dione and Madagascin, both of which ultimately target Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates that Tumonoic acid C may influence Phosphodiesterase 6C via multiple indirect pathways, possibly through the Leukocyte antigen CD37 protein. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Tumonoic acid C modulates the activity of CD37, which then serves as a bridge to Phosphodiesterase 6C. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain. The presence of multiple targets and pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship and the need for further experimental validation.",
